          "filename": "RAF Fylingdales pre-1992 - geograph.org.uk - 80681.jpg",
          "caption": "RAF Fylingdales pre-1992. Opened in 1962, RAF Fylingdales is primarily a ballistic missile early warning station, with a secondary duty of detecting, reporting and tracking satellite launches and orbits. The famous \"golf ball\" radomes seen here were replaced between 1989 and 1992 by the pyramid - like Solid State Phased Array Radar (SSPAR), which became operational in October 1992. A 'before' picture to go with the one already uploaded for this square. 47117",
